SUMMARY:The Healing WELL Fundraiser: Figaro Up\, Figaro Down
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T143000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17772765@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Celebrating The Healing WELL’s annual fundraiser at the Roxi
 e\, “The Power of the Second Act.”\n\nFeaturing panel discussion after
  the film with director Javid Soriano and Tim Blevins!\n\nA Juilliard-trai
 ned baritone\, Tim Blevins performed on the world’s most prestigious ope
 ra stages\, tackling challenging roles with skill and power. A rare Black 
 presence in a white-dominated art form\, he rose to fame—but lost everyt
 hing to addiction: his career\, family\, and home\, leaving him unhoused i
 n the Tenderloin. After decades in despair\, Blevins takes control of his 
 destiny\, staging a comeback that restores not only his place on stage but
  also his role in his family’s life. Filmed with care and grace\, this S
 an Francisco-set tale of fame\, loss\, and redemption illuminates a life a
 s remarkable as the operas he mastered. —Bedatri Choudhury\n\nRuntime\n\
 n1h 15m\n\nYear\n\n2026\n\nDirector\n\nJavid Soriano\n\nFormat\n\nDCP\n\nF
 irst Showing\n\nOctober 4\, 2026\n\nCategories\n\nFeatured\n\nDetails: htt
 ps://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/4/the-healing-well-fundraiser-figaro-up-f
 igaro-down-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7647103;-122.4224081
