DESCRIPTION:Filmmaker Colette Ghunim in person for post-screening Q&A on F
 riday\, October 2!\n\nFilmed over five years and featuring evocative anima
 tion and archival footage\, Traces of Home is a meditation on memory and a
 n unflinching look at what it takes to find our way back home to ourselves
 . From filmmaker Colette Ghunim\, Traces of Home is an extraordinary journ
 ey of self-discovery\, following Ghunim as she undertakes a quest to reuni
 te her parents with the ancestral homes they were forced to flee as childr
 en in Palestine and Mexico.\n\n“A stunning debut for filmmaker Colette G
 hunim.” —Lapacazo Sandoval\, Amsterdam News\n\n“A poignant and emoti
 onally resonant exploration of the multiple ways that unspoken pain transf
 ers between generations.” —Eleanor Bader\, The Indypendent\n\n“If yo
 u want to see something you haven’t seen before\, give Traces of Home a 
 shot.” —Steve Kopian\, Unseen Films\n\nDOC NYC – Winner of Grand Jur
 y Prize\n\nMore showtimes to be announced.\n\nRuntime\n\n1h 33m\n\nYear\n\
 n2026\n\nDirector\n\nColette Ghunim\n\nFormat\n\nDCP\n\nCountry\n\nUSA\n\n
 Language\n\nEnglish\, Arabic\, and Spanish with English subtitles\n\nFirst
  Showing\n\nOctober 2\, 2026\n\nCategories\n\nBay Visions\n\n\,\n\nFeature
 d\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/22166?siteToken=
 4m48btf3yavn7xjk5yxk6nc40c\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/5
 /traces-of-home-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7647103;-122.4224081
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
