CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Elephant Gym successfully completed a world tour spanning 60 c
 ities across 23 countries. However\, behind this achievement lay an unseen
  crisis of disbandment\, along with hidden conflicts and struggles. What d
 oes it truly mean to be a band?\n\nThe film was first screened in October 
 2025 at the Kaohsiung Film Festival\, one of Taiwans leading film festival
 s\, and will also be shown in theaters in both Japan and Taiwan. While the
 ir world tour across 23 countries and 60 cities was a major success\, the 
 film reveals the untold story behind itincluding a looming breakup crisis 
 during its preparation\, as well as the bands internal conflicts and strug
 gles.\n\nIf your dreams were to become reality\, what price would you be w
 illing to pay?\n\nElephant Gym\, an instrumental band from Kaohsiung\, Tai
 wan\, has been creating indie music since its formation in 2012. Their sou
 nd blends complex rhythms with irregular time signatures and sophisticated
  melodies. In Taiwan\, their avant-garde musical style often raised the qu
 estion: who would even listen to this?\n\nHowever\, in 2024\, they embarke
 d on a world tour covering 23 countries and 60 shows\, including three per
 formances in the Philippines. They captivated audiences worldwide and firm
 ly established their presence. Yet behind the glamorous stage\, there were
  deep struggles.\n\nBetween guitarist Tell Chang and bassist KT Changwho a
 re siblingsthere were conflicts between family ties and band dynamics. Dru
 mmer Chia-Chin Tu had to make the difficult decision to l...\n\nTickets: h
 ttps://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/19867?siteToken=d2atbcege5knqsa
 vntt91g1250\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/11/elephant-gym-
 more-real-than-dreams-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
