BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Tale of Two Sisters
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T131500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T151500
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17830865@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:If you think about it long enough\, anything can be supernatur
 al – your toothbrush\, a pair of sneakers\, or your parents. That’s wh
 at makes A TALE OF TWO SISTERS so terrifying. Sisters Soo-mi and Soo-yeon 
 arrive at their father’s country home to spend some quality time with th
 eir new stepmother. But there’s trouble in paradise. For proof\, check o
 ut the severed hands that live in a kitchen cabinet. The first Korean horr
 or movie to be distributed in America\, A TALE OF TWO SISTERS is a beautif
 ul hallucinogen. It’s quiet\, violent\, and visually stunning\, feeling 
 like a Korean version of THE SHINING as filtered through the adolescent pr
 e-angst of a Judy Blume novel if Judy Blume was secretly a demon. You’ll
  never see another haunted house movie like this one – and you’ll neve
 r forget it. (Joseph A. Ziemba)\n\nTickets: https://drafthouse.com/sf/show
 /sad-girl-cinema-club-a-tale-of-two-sisters?cinemaId=0802&sessionId=21343\
 nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/18/a-tale-of-two-sisters-tic
 kets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7562198;-122.419185
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34368038/0dd30207-3a70-47e6-b35b-d4fdd6e92a0b.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:Alamo Drafthouse Cinema\, 2550 Mission St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 
 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
